          },
          "looks": [
            {
              "at": "flame",
              "before": "A silvery strip of metal is held in tongs, beside the burner.",
              "after": "The strip burns with a white light, too bright to look at."
            },
            {
              "at": "solid",
              "before": "Only the strip is in the tongs.",
              "after": "The strip is gone. A white powder is left where it was."
            }
          ],
          "kind": {
            "value": "combination",
            "sourceId": "soult-types-of-inorganic-reactions"
          },
          "equation": {
            "reactants": [
              {
                "speciesId": "magnesium",
                "coefficient": 2
              },
              {
                "speciesId": "oxygen",
                "coefficient": 1
              }
            ],
            "products": [
              {
                "speciesId": "magnesium-oxide",
                "coefficient": 2
              }
            ],
            "sourceId": "soult-types-of-inorganic-reactions"
          }
        }
      ],
      "order": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "value": "Magnesium joined with oxygen from the air and made magnesium oxide, a white powder. Two things became one: a combination.",
          "sourceId": "soult-types-of-inorganic-reactions"
        },
        {
          "value": "Burnt in air, magnesium also joins with the air's nitrogen, so the ash is a mixture: magnesium oxide with magnesium nitride in it. The equation here is for the oxide alone.",
          "sourceId": "chemguide-group2-oxygen"
        }
      ]
    },
